{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785183896,"nonce":"p5P9TRqi5bjq1faCvPkzq0X9gmo=","title":"ADR-0062 (deferred): fuse a linear Step chain into one Pod so the boundary disappears","message":"Attack boundary **count** rather than boundary **cost**. Automatically co-locate a linear chain of Steps into one Pod when their placement profiles match and no gate or approval intervenes, so no workspace bytes move between them at all.\n\nDistinct from ADR-0061's rejected \"coarsening the unit\", which is an *authoring* change — this is invisible to the author. Not rejected on merit; deferred because it trades away per-Step restart granularity inside a fused group, which collides with ADR-0027 and ADR-0056 and would have to be governed and visible in the UI.\n\n\n- [ ] Design recorded before any code: what makes a chain fusable, and what a Rerun of a step inside a fused group means\n- [ ] Fusion is visible in the UI — a user must be able to see why a step has no boundary of its own\n- [ ] Never fuses across a gate, an approval, or a placement-profile change\n\n\nNone - but deliberately deferred; do not start without a decision","files":null}]}